    "result_text": "All 260 tests pass. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` \u2192 shared `householdId` feature. The household-uniqueness guard (rejecting a same-lastName/same-address owner unless `sharesHousehold` is true) already existed; the new piece was assigning and returning a stable shared `householdId`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `household_id` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`hsqldb` \u2014 used by tests, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it.\n\n4. **New OfficeFloor step `AssignHouseholdId`** (`function/owner/AssignHouseholdId.java`) \u2014 when the request sets `sharesHousehold` true, it finds existing owners in the same household (same last name + address, normalized case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace, matching `EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique`), computes a **deterministic** identifier (12-char upper-hex SHA-256 prefix over the normalized last name + address), assigns it to the new owner, and back-fills any household member that lacks one. Determinism makes it stable across joins and guarantees every member shares the same value; if a member already has an id, that value is reused.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted the `assignHousehold` step (under `transaction` governance) between `assignCustomerCode` and `save`.\n\n6. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"householdId\", ignore = true)` to `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (mirroring the existing `customerCode` ignore); `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` auto-maps the field.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`, the V1 owner tests, and the full suite (260 tests) all pass.",
